From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: depth bias

The rasterizer state copied DepthBias, SlopeScaledDepthBias and DepthBiasClamp but never enabled polygon offset
(offset_tri/line/point), so no bias was ever applied: shadow maps drawn with one shadowed their own casters (acne).
D3D biases every primitive type and fill mode, so all three are on when either bias is set.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Rasterizer.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Rasterizer.cpp
index ea0b256..9e3cfab 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Rasterizer.cpp
@@ -233,6 +233,10 @@ CreateRasterizerStateForced(D3D10DDI_HDEVICE hDevice, const D3D10_DDI_RASTERIZER
    state.offset_units = (float)pRasterizerDesc->DepthBias;
    state.offset_scale = pRasterizerDesc->SlopeScaledDepthBias;
    state.offset_clamp = pRasterizerDesc->DepthBiasClamp;
+   /* Without these the bias was never applied: shadow maps drawn with one shadow their own casters (acne). D3D
+    * biases every primitive type and fill mode. */
+   state.offset_tri = state.offset_line = state.offset_point =
+      pRasterizerDesc->DepthBias != 0 || pRasterizerDesc->SlopeScaledDepthBias != 0.0f;
    /* As feature level 10_1 and up: MultisampleEnable only picks the line algorithm, triangles on multisampled
     * targets are always multisampled (10_0 left them aliased without it). No effect on single-sampled targets. */
    state.multisample = 1;
